      <string id="Cat_Agent">RemoteHub Agent</string>
      <string id="Cat_Agent_Help">Settings of the RemoteHub Agent service on this device: who may do what on it, through the agent.

They are read from HKLM\Software\Policies\RemoteHub\Agent for every connection, so a change applies without restarting the service, and they win over the agent's agent.json. If the key exists but can't be read, the agent allows nothing until it can.

On a device with RemoteHub installed too, these policies don't affect what RemoteHub on this device may do on other devices: that is the category RemoteHub Console.</string>
      <string id="Cat_Agent_Features">Features</string>
      <string id="Cat_Agent_Rights">Access rights</string>
      <string id="Cat_Agent_Desktop">Remote desktop</string>
      <string id="Cat_Agent_Consent">Consent</string>
      <string id="Cat_Agent_Privacy">Privacy</string>
      <string id="Cat_Agent_AutoSignIn">Automatic sign-in</string>
      <string id="Cat_Agent_JumpHost">Jump host</string>
      <string id="Cat_Agent_Broker">RemoteHub Broker</string>
      <string id="Cat_Agent_Service">Service</string>

      <!-- Console -->
      <string id="Console_SettingsFolder">Shared settings folder</string>
      <string id="Console_SettingsFolder_Help">The folder where RemoteHub keeps its shared, encrypted settings file (folders, connections, credentials), for example %OneDriveCommercial%\RemoteHub or a network share. Environment variables are allowed.

Enabled: RemoteHub uses this folder, and users can't change the location. Each PC asks once for the settings file's password.

Disabled or Not configured: the user chooses where the settings are kept (this PC or a shared folder).

Registry: SettingsFolder (REG_EXPAND_SZ). The older key Software\Policies\RdpManager is still read.</string>

      <string id="Console_DisableUpdateCheck">Turn off the update check</string>
      <string id="Console_DisableUpdateCheck_Help">Enabled: RemoteHub never contacts the update server, for example when updates come through software deployment. The setting is greyed out in RemoteHub.

Disabled: RemoteHub checks for updates, and users can't turn it off (since 0.19.0; before, Disabled meant Not configured).

Not configured: the user decides in Settings → Updates &amp; privacy.

Registry: DisableUpdateCheck (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_UpdateChannel">Update channel</string>
      <string id="Console_UpdateChannel_Help">Fixes the channel RemoteHub looks for updates in: GA (stable releases) or Beta (pre-releases). The choice is greyed out in RemoteHub.

Disabled or Not configured: the user decides. The default is Beta for versions below 1.0 and pre-releases, otherwise GA.

Registry: UpdateChannel (REG_SZ) = stable or beta.</string>
      <string id="Console_UpdateChannel_Stable">GA – stable releases</string>
      <string id="Console_UpdateChannel_Beta">Beta – pre-releases</string>

      <string id="Console_DisableTelemetry">Turn off usage data and crash reports</string>
      <string id="Console_DisableTelemetry_Help">Enabled: RemoteHub sends no anonymous usage data and no crash reports. The setting is greyed out in RemoteHub.

Disabled: RemoteHub sends usage data and crash reports, and users can't turn it off (since 0.19.0; before, Disabled meant Not configured). The privacy statement describes what is sent.

Not configured: the user decides in Settings → Updates &amp; privacy (on by default).

The RemoteHub Agent never sends usage data.

Registry: DisableTelemetry (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_DisableRecording">Turn off recording</string>
      <string id="Console_DisableRecording_Help">Enabled: tabs can't be recorded. The Record button isn't shown, and the recording settings are greyed out.

Disabled or Not configured: users can record tabs.

Registry: DisableRecording (REG_DWORD) = 1.</string>

      <string id="Console_RecordingFolder">Recording folder</string>
      <string id="Console_RecordingFolder_Help">The folder where recordings are saved. Environment variables are allowed, for example %USERPROFILE%\Videos\RemoteHub or a network share.

Enabled: recordings go to this folder, and users can't change it.

Disabled or Not configured: the user chooses (default: Videos\RemoteHub).

Registry: RecordingFolder (REG_EXPAND_SZ).</string>

      <string id="Console_AuditRetentionDays">Keep audit log entries</string>
      <string id="Console_AuditRetentionDays_Help">How many days RemoteHub's audit log on this PC keeps its entries (1–36500). Older entries are removed when RemoteHub starts.

Enabled: this number of days; the setting is greyed out in Settings → Logs.

Disabled or Not configured: the user decides (default 365 days).

Registry: AuditRetentionDays (REG_DWORD).</string>

      <string id="Console_DisableAgentAutoSignIn">Turn off automatic sign-in through the agent</string>
      <string id="Console_DisableAgentAutoSignIn_Help">Enabled: RemoteHub never signs in automatically on a device where nobody is signed in. The connection setting "Sign in automatically when nobody is signed in" is greyed out.

Disabled or Not configured: users can turn it on per connection. The device must allow it too: RemoteHub Agent → Automatic sign-in.

Registry: DisableAgentAutoSignIn (REG_DWORD) = 1.</string>

      <!-- Console: features -->
      <string id="Console_AllowRdp">Allow remote desktop over RDP</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowRdp_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: RemoteHub doesn't open RDP sessions. The RDP entries in the menus aren't shown, and opening a connection, a .rdp file or a reconnect over RDP is refused with "Remote desktop over RDP is turned off by your organisation". Remote desktop through the RemoteHub Agent isn't affected.

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only. To stop RDP to a device, turn RDP off on the device.

Registry: AllowRdp (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowAgent">Allow the RemoteHub Agent</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowAgent_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: RemoteHub doesn't use the RemoteHub Agent at all: no remote desktop, tools, installation or automatic sign-in through it, and no jump hosts, whatever the other policies in this category say. The connection settings "Connect through" and "Remote desktop through" are greyed out; the tools go over PowerShell remoting and the remote desktop over RDP.

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only. What the agent allows on a device is decided by the device's own policy: RemoteHub Agent → Features and Remote desktop.

Registry: AllowAgent (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowAgentDesktop">Allow remote desktop through the agent</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowAgentDesktop_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: Remote desktop through the RemoteHub Agent isn't offered, and opening it is refused. Connections set to it use RDP. The connection settings "Remote desktop through" and the automatic sign-in settings are greyed out.

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only. On the device: RemoteHub Agent → Remote desktop → "Allow remote desktop" (DesktopEnabled).

Registry: AllowAgentDesktop (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowAgentPowerShell">Allow PowerShell through the agent</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowAgentPowerShell_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: The PowerShell tab isn't offered for connections that use the RemoteHub Agent, and opening it is refused. Over PowerShell remoting it depends on "Allow PowerShell over WinRM".

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only. On the device: RemoteHub Agent → Features → "Allow PowerShell, files, registry, services and processes" (PowerShellEnabled). The agent can't block the tools one by one.

Registry: AllowAgentPowerShell (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowAgentFileTransfer">Allow file transfer through the agent</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowAgentFileTransfer_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: The file transfer tab isn't offered for connections that use the RemoteHub Agent, and opening it or dropping files on a PowerShell tab is refused. Over PowerShell remoting it depends on "Allow file transfer over WinRM".

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only. On the device: RemoteHub Agent → Features → "Allow PowerShell, files, registry, services and processes" (PowerShellEnabled). The agent can't block the tools one by one.

Registry: AllowAgentFileTransfer (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowAgentRegistry">Allow the registry through the agent</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowAgentRegistry_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: The registry tab isn't offered for connections that use the RemoteHub Agent, and opening it is refused. Over PowerShell remoting it depends on "Allow the registry over WinRM".

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only. On the device: RemoteHub Agent → Features → "Allow PowerShell, files, registry, services and processes" (PowerShellEnabled). The agent can't block the tools one by one.

Registry: AllowAgentRegistry (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowAgentServices">Allow services through the agent</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowAgentServices_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: The services tab isn't offered for connections that use the RemoteHub Agent, and opening it is refused. Over PowerShell remoting it depends on "Allow services over WinRM".

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only. On the device: RemoteHub Agent → Features → "Allow PowerShell, files, registry, services and processes" (PowerShellEnabled). The agent can't block the tools one by one.

Registry: AllowAgentServices (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowAgentProcesses">Allow processes through the agent</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowAgentProcesses_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: The processes tab isn't offered for connections that use the RemoteHub Agent, and opening it is refused. Over PowerShell remoting it depends on "Allow processes over WinRM".

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only. On the device: RemoteHub Agent → Features → "Allow PowerShell, files, registry, services and processes" (PowerShellEnabled). The agent can't block the tools one by one.

Registry: AllowAgentProcesses (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowBroker">Allow the RemoteHub Broker</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowBroker_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: RemoteHub on this PC doesn't connect to a RemoteHub Broker – Settings → RemoteHub Broker is locked, the synced folders of brokers aren't kept up to date, and devices in them are reached only directly (Reach: Direct).

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only. On the device: RemoteHub Agent → RemoteHub Broker → "Allow the RemoteHub Broker" (BrokerEnabled).</string>
      <string id="Console_BrokerDirect">Direct connections through the RemoteHub Broker</string>
      <string id="Console_BrokerDirect_Help">Enabled or Not configured: a session through the RemoteHub Broker also tries a direct connection to the device (UDP, hole punching, QUIC), and uses it when it comes up – faster than the relay. The device's certificate pin and the Windows sign-in apply as on the relay.

Disabled: RemoteHub on this PC never tries the direct path; every session through the broker is relayed (TCP 443 to the broker only).

On the device: RemoteHub Agent → RemoteHub Broker → "Direct connections through the broker" (BrokerDirect).

Registry: BrokerDirect (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowAgentEventLog">Allow the event viewer through the agent</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowAgentEventLog_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: The Event Viewer tab isn't offered for connections that use the RemoteHub Agent, and opening it is refused. Over PowerShell remoting it depends on "Allow the event viewer over WinRM".

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only. On the device: RemoteHub Agent → Features → "Allow PowerShell, files, registry, services and processes" (PowerShellEnabled). The agent can't block the tools one by one.

Registry: AllowAgentEventLog (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowAgentScheduledTasks">Allow scheduled tasks through the agent</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowAgentScheduledTasks_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: The Scheduled tasks tab isn't offered for connections that use the RemoteHub Agent, and opening it is refused. Over PowerShell remoting it depends on "Allow scheduled tasks over WinRM".

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only. On the device: RemoteHub Agent → Features → "Allow PowerShell, files, registry, services and processes" (PowerShellEnabled). The agent can't block the tools one by one.

Registry: AllowAgentScheduledTasks (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowAgentDeviceActions">Allow device actions through the agent</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowAgentDeviceActions_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: The Device actions in a connection's menu – lock, send a message, sign out, restart, shut down, update Group Policy and sync with Intune – aren't offered for connections that use the RemoteHub Agent, and starting one is refused. Over PowerShell remoting it depends on "Allow device actions over WinRM".

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only. On the device: RemoteHub Agent → Features → "Allow PowerShell, files, registry, services and processes" (PowerShellEnabled) – the actions run as PowerShell commands of the account that signs in. The agent can't block them one by one.

Registry: AllowAgentDeviceActions (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowAgentInstall">Allow installing and updating the agent</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowAgentInstall_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: Install RemoteHub Agent… and Update RemoteHub Agent… aren't offered, for every method – for organisations that deploy the agent with Intune or Configuration Manager.

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only.

Registry: AllowAgentInstall (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowCredentialProviderInstall">Allow installing and removing the credential provider</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowCredentialProviderInstall_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: Install credential provider and Remove credential provider aren't offered, and the install dialog's "Allow automatic sign-in" is greyed out.

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only. On the device: RemoteHub Agent → Automatic sign-in → "When nobody is signed in" (NoUserBehavior).

Registry: AllowCredentialProviderInstall (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowPowerShellRemoting">Allow PowerShell remoting (WinRM)</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowPowerShellRemoting_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: RemoteHub doesn't use PowerShell remoting at all: no tools over it, no remoting check or test, no setup script, and no agent installation over it, whatever the other policies in this category say. The connection settings "Check automatically after RDP login" and "Use HTTPS" are greyed out. Connections that use the RemoteHub Agent aren't affected.

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only. To stop WinRM to a device, turn it off on the device.

Registry: AllowPowerShellRemoting (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowRemotingPowerShell">Allow PowerShell over WinRM</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowRemotingPowerShell_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: The PowerShell tab isn't offered for connections that use PowerShell remoting, and opening it is refused. Through the agent it depends on "Allow PowerShell through the agent".

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only.

Registry: AllowRemotingPowerShell (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowRemotingFileTransfer">Allow file transfer over WinRM</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowRemotingFileTransfer_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: The file transfer tab isn't offered for connections that use PowerShell remoting, and opening it or dropping files on a PowerShell tab is refused. Through the agent it depends on "Allow file transfer through the agent".

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only.

Registry: AllowRemotingFileTransfer (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowRemotingRegistry">Allow the registry over WinRM</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowRemotingRegistry_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: The registry tab isn't offered for connections that use PowerShell remoting, and opening it is refused. Through the agent it depends on "Allow the registry through the agent".

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only.

Registry: AllowRemotingRegistry (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowRemotingServices">Allow services over WinRM</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowRemotingServices_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: The services tab isn't offered for connections that use PowerShell remoting, and opening it is refused. Through the agent it depends on "Allow services through the agent".

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only.

Registry: AllowRemotingServices (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowRemotingProcesses">Allow processes over WinRM</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowRemotingProcesses_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: The processes tab isn't offered for connections that use PowerShell remoting, and opening it is refused. Through the agent it depends on "Allow processes through the agent".

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only.

Registry: AllowRemotingProcesses (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowRemotingEventLog">Allow the event viewer over WinRM</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowRemotingEventLog_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: The Event Viewer tab isn't offered for connections that use PowerShell remoting, and opening it is refused. Through the agent it depends on "Allow the event viewer through the agent".

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only.

Registry: AllowRemotingEventLog (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowRemotingScheduledTasks">Allow scheduled tasks over WinRM</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowRemotingScheduledTasks_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: The Scheduled tasks tab isn't offered for connections that use PowerShell remoting, and opening it is refused. Through the agent it depends on "Allow scheduled tasks through the agent".

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only.

Registry: AllowRemotingScheduledTasks (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowRemotingDeviceActions">Allow device actions over WinRM</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowRemotingDeviceActions_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: The Device actions in a connection's menu – lock, send a message, sign out, restart, shut down, update Group Policy and sync with Intune – aren't offered for connections that use PowerShell remoting, and starting one is refused. Through the agent it depends on "Allow device actions through the agent".

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only.

Registry: AllowRemotingDeviceActions (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowRemotingSetup">Allow setting up PowerShell remoting on a target</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowRemotingSetup_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: Set up PowerShell remoting on the target… isn't offered, and the remoting test doesn't offer the setup script.

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only.

Registry: AllowRemotingSetup (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowQuickConnect">Allow quick connect to a typed address</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowQuickConnect_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: Typing a name or address that isn't a saved connection in the search box (Ctrl+F) and pressing Enter doesn't connect. Saved connections still open.

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only.

Registry: AllowQuickConnect (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowJumpHosts">Allow jump hosts</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowJumpHosts_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: Connections below a jump host don't connect, Move under isn't shown, and items can't be dragged below a connection. They stay in the tree. Also off when "Allow the RemoteHub Agent" is disabled, because a jump host is an agent.

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only. On the jump host: RemoteHub Agent → Jump host → "Allow this device as a jump host" (TunnelEnabled).

Registry: AllowJumpHosts (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowNetworkShares">Allow network shares</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowNetworkShares_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: Network shares can't be added or opened, whatever the policies for the single protocols say. Shares already in the tree stay there.

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only.

Registry: AllowNetworkShares (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowSmb">Allow SMB shares</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowSmb_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: SMB shares can't be opened; they stay in the tree. "Allow network shares" disabled wins over this.

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only.

Registry: AllowSmb (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowSftp">Allow SFTP shares</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowSftp_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: SFTP shares can't be opened; they stay in the tree. "Allow network shares" disabled wins over this.

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only.

Registry: AllowSftp (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowFtp">Allow FTP shares</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowFtp_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: FTP shares can't be opened; they stay in the tree. "Allow network shares" disabled wins over this.

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only.

Registry: AllowFtp (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowWebDav">Allow WebDAV shares</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowWebDav_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: WebDAV shares can't be opened; they stay in the tree. "Allow network shares" disabled wins over this.

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only.

Registry: AllowWebDav (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowRdpFileImport">Allow importing .rdp files</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowRdpFileImport_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: Import .rdp files… isn't shown, and .rdp files dropped on RemoteHub or opened with it aren't imported.

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only.

Registry: AllowRdpFileImport (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowRdpFileExport">Allow saving .rdp files</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowRdpFileExport_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: Save as .rdp file… and Export folder as .rdp files… aren't shown.

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only.

Registry: AllowRdpFileExport (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowBackupExport">Allow exporting a backup</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowBackupExport_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: Export backup… isn't shown. A backup holds every stored password.

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only.

Registry: AllowBackupExport (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowBackupImport">Allow importing a backup</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowBackupImport_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: Import backup… isn't shown.

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only.

Registry: AllowBackupImport (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowNotes">Allow Notes</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowNotes_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: the Notes view isn't shown. The view rail has no Notes item, Ctrl+2 and links to pages do nothing, and the connection tree's Notes command isn't shown. Notes already stored on this PC are kept, not deleted: they come back when the policy is removed, and backups still include them.

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only.

Registry: AllowNotes (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowScripts">Allow Scripts</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowScripts_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: the Scripts view isn't shown. The view rail has no Scripts item, Ctrl+3 does nothing, and no "Run script" command is offered. Scripts already stored on this PC are kept, not deleted: they come back when the policy is removed, and backups still include them.

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only.

Registry: AllowScripts (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowScriptRun">Allow running scripts on devices</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowScriptRun_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: PowerShell scripts can be written, kept and exported, but not run on a device: "Run script" and "Run on" aren't offered. A run is the PowerShell tool used another way, so it also needs PowerShell through the agent or over WinRM (whichever the connection uses) to be allowed.

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only. On a device with the RemoteHub Agent, the agent's own policy (PowerShell and its access right) decides too.

Registry: AllowScriptRun (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowScriptRunSystem">Allow running scripts as System</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowScriptRunSystem_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: scripts can't run as NT AUTHORITY\SYSTEM on a device (a one-off scheduled task), and so not as "Both" either.

Registry: AllowScriptRunSystem (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowScriptRunUser">Allow running scripts as the signed-in user</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowScriptRunUser_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: scripts can't run as the user signed in on a device (a one-off scheduled task in their session), and so not as "Both" either.

Registry: AllowScriptRunUser (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowScriptRunAsMe">Allow running scripts as the connection's account</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowScriptRunAsMe_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: scripts can't run as the account RemoteHub signs in with ("As me"), which the script library uses for Active Directory and server administration.

Registry: AllowScriptRunAsMe (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowScriptDraftRun">Allow testing a draft on a device</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowScriptDraftRun_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: only versions marked "Ready to deploy" can run on devices; "Test draft on" isn't offered.

Registry: AllowScriptDraftRun (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowScriptLibrary">Allow the built-in script library</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowScriptLibrary_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: the Scripts view doesn't show the library that comes with RemoteHub, and its scripts can't be run. The organisation's own scripts are still allowed, including copies made from the library before.

Registry: AllowScriptLibrary (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowScriptImport">Allow importing scripts</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowScriptImport_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: script files, folders and script packages (.rhscripts) can't be imported into the Scripts view.

Registry: AllowScriptImport (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowScriptExport">Allow exporting scripts</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowScriptExport_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: scripts can't be saved as files or exported as script packages (.rhscripts). Copying a script's text is still possible.

Registry: AllowScriptExport (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AllowSharedSettings">Allow a shared settings folder</string>
      <string id="Console_AllowSharedSettings_Help">Enabled or Not configured: allowed.

Disabled: Users can't choose a shared settings folder; a folder already in use stays until they switch to this PC only. The policy "Shared settings folder" still applies.

This binds RemoteHub on this PC only.

Registry: AllowSharedSettings (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <!-- Console: settings and connection settings -->
      <string id="Console_Theme">Theme</string>
      <string id="Console_Theme_Help">Fixes this setting of RemoteHub on this PC. It is greyed out in Settings → General and users can't change it.

Enabled: the value chosen here.

Disabled or Not configured: the user decides (default: Dark).

Registry: Theme (REG_SZ: Dark, Light, System).</string>
