      <string id="Console_AgentDesktopQuality">Picture</string>
      <string id="Console_AgentDesktopQuality_Help">Fixes this setting of RemoteHub on this PC. It is greyed out in the agent desktop's start panel and toolbar and users can't change it.

Enabled: the value chosen here.

Disabled or Not configured: the user decides (default: Admin work – 30 fps).

The device's MaxFramesPerSecond and MaxQuality still cap it.

Registry: AgentDesktopQuality (REG_SZ: Low, Admin, High, Smooth).</string>
      <string id="Console_AgentDesktopQuality_Low">Slow connection – 15 fps</string>
      <string id="Console_AgentDesktopQuality_Admin">Admin work – 30 fps</string>
      <string id="Console_AgentDesktopQuality_High">Sharp – 30 fps, best picture</string>
      <string id="Console_AgentDesktopQuality_Smooth">Smooth – 60 fps, best picture</string>

      <string id="Console_AgentDesktopConsent">How the signed-in user is asked</string>
      <string id="Console_AgentDesktopConsent_Help">Fixes this setting of RemoteHub on this PC. It is greyed out in the agent desktop's start panel and users can't change it.

Enabled: the value chosen here.

Disabled or Not configured: the user decides (default: the last one used).

The device's AllowedConsentModes still decide what it accepts: a mode the device doesn't offer leaves the choice to the user.

Registry: AgentDesktopConsent (REG_SZ: Ask, Pin, None).</string>
      <string id="Console_AgentDesktopConsent_Ask">Ask them to allow it</string>
      <string id="Console_AgentDesktopConsent_Pin">Show them a code</string>
      <string id="Console_AgentDesktopConsent_None">Connect without asking</string>

      <string id="Console_AgentDesktopViewOnly">Always view only</string>
      <string id="Console_AgentDesktopViewOnly_Help">Fixes this setting of RemoteHub on this PC. It is greyed out in the agent desktop's start panel and users can't change it.

Enabled: every agent desktop is view only: no mouse and keyboard, no clipboard.

Disabled: users can control the device when the device allows it.

Not configured: the user decides (default: the user decides).

Registry: AgentDesktopViewOnly (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AgentDesktopFitToWindow">Fit the device's resolution to the window</string>
      <string id="Console_AgentDesktopFitToWindow_Help">Fixes this setting of RemoteHub on this PC. It is greyed out in the agent desktop's toolbar and users can't change it.

Enabled: the device's resolution follows the RemoteHub window.

Disabled: the device keeps its own resolution.

Not configured: the user decides (default: fit to the window).

Registry: AgentDesktopFitToWindow (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AgentDesktopShowInfo">Show connection details</string>
      <string id="Console_AgentDesktopShowInfo_Help">Fixes this setting of RemoteHub on this PC. It is greyed out in the agent desktop's toolbar and users can't change it.

Enabled: frames, data rate, round trip and quality are shown.

Disabled: they aren't shown.

Not configured: the user decides (default: off).

Registry: AgentDesktopShowInfo (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AgentDesktopKeyCombinations">Send Windows key combinations</string>
      <string id="Console_AgentDesktopKeyCombinations_Help">Fixes this setting of RemoteHub on this PC. It is greyed out in the agent desktop's toolbar and users can't change it.

Enabled: Alt+Tab, the Windows key and other combinations go to the device while the tab has the focus.

Disabled: they stay on this PC.

Not configured: the user decides (default: on).

Registry: AgentDesktopKeyCombinations (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_AgentDesktopClipboard">Clipboard</string>
      <string id="Console_AgentDesktopClipboard_Help">Limits what the clipboard of an agent desktop started from RemoteHub on this PC may carry.

Enabled: the value chosen here.

Disabled or Not configured: the user decides (default: text, images and files).

The lower of this and the device's DesktopClipboard applies.

Registry: AgentDesktopClipboard (REG_DWORD: 0, 1, 2, 3).</string>
      <string id="Console_AgentDesktopClipboard_0">Off</string>
      <string id="Console_AgentDesktopClipboard_1">Text</string>
      <string id="Console_AgentDesktopClipboard_2">Text and images</string>
      <string id="Console_AgentDesktopClipboard_3">Text, images and files</string>

      <string id="Console_InstallMethods">Install methods offered</string>
      <string id="Console_InstallMethods_Help">A default of RemoteHub's Install / Update RemoteHub Agent dialog on this PC, greyed out there so users can't change it.

Enabled: the values set here.

Disabled or Not configured: the user decides (default: all four).

One per line: Remoting (silently over PowerShell remoting), ThroughAgent (update through the running agent), Clipboard (copy the files into an RDP session), SaveFiles (save the files for software distribution). Methods not in the list are greyed out.

Registry: Methods (REG_MULTI_SZ).</string>

      <string id="Console_InstallPort">Port</string>
      <string id="Console_InstallPort_Help">A default of RemoteHub's Install / Update RemoteHub Agent dialog on this PC, greyed out there so users can't change it.

Enabled: the value set here (TCP port).

Disabled or Not configured: the user decides (default: 58732).

Written into the enrollment file. Must match the agent's ListenPort policy if one is set; the device's policy wins.

Registry: Port (REG_DWORD), 1–65535.</string>

      <string id="Console_InstallFirewallScope">Allow connections from</string>
      <string id="Console_InstallFirewallScope_Help">A default of RemoteHub's Install / Update RemoteHub Agent dialog on this PC, greyed out there so users can't change it.

Enabled: the value set here.

Disabled or Not configured: the user decides (default: any address).

The scope of the agent's firewall rule: addresses and ranges, comma-separated, for example 10.1.0.0/16, 192.168.1.20. Empty means any address.

Registry: FirewallScope (REG_SZ).</string>

      <string id="Console_InstallAllowedGroups">Allowed accounts</string>
      <string id="Console_InstallAllowedGroups_Help">A default of RemoteHub's Install / Update RemoteHub Agent dialog on this PC, greyed out there so users can't change it.

Enabled: the values set here.

Disabled or Not configured: the user decides (default: Administrators).

One group name or SID per line, written into the enrollment file. The device's Rights policy wins over it.

Registry: AllowedGroups (REG_MULTI_SZ).</string>

      <string id="Console_InstallVirtualDisplay">Virtual display for servers without a monitor</string>
      <string id="Console_InstallVirtualDisplay_Help">A default of RemoteHub's Install / Update RemoteHub Agent dialog on this PC, greyed out there so users can't change it.

Enabled: the install option is ticked.

Disabled: the install option is unticked.

Not configured: the user decides (default: on).

Registry: VirtualDisplay (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_InstallAutoSignIn">Allow automatic sign-in</string>
      <string id="Console_InstallAutoSignIn_Help">A default of RemoteHub's Install / Update RemoteHub Agent dialog on this PC, greyed out there so users can't change it.

Enabled: the install option is ticked (only for the silent methods, and only when "Allow installing and removing the credential provider" isn't disabled).

Disabled: the install option is unticked, so a silent install leaves the credential provider out (AUTOSIGNIN=0) and an update removes it.

Not configured: the user decides (default: on). The other install methods run the MSI by hand, which installs the credential provider unless AUTOSIGNIN=0 is added to its command line.

Registry: AutoSignIn (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_InstallUseAgentAfterwards">Use the agent for the connection afterwards</string>
      <string id="Console_InstallUseAgentAfterwards_Help">A default of RemoteHub's Install / Update RemoteHub Agent dialog on this PC, greyed out there so users can't change it.

Enabled: the connection switches to the agent after the install.

Disabled: the connection keeps working the way it did.

Not configured: the user decides (default: on).

Registry: UseAgentAfterwards (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_ConnResize">Resize behaviour</string>
      <string id="Console_ConnResize_Help">Fixes this setting for every connection on this PC. It wins over the global defaults, the folders and the connection, which keep their own value but don't use it; the connection editor shows it greyed out at every level. A settings file shared with PCs without this policy keeps working there as before.

Enabled: the value chosen here.

Disabled or Not configured: the user decides (default: Dynamic resolution).

Registry: Resize (REG_SZ: DynamicResolution, SmartSizing, Fixed).</string>
      <string id="Console_ConnResize_DynamicResolution">Dynamic resolution</string>
      <string id="Console_ConnResize_SmartSizing">Smart sizing (scale)</string>
      <string id="Console_ConnResize_Fixed">Fixed resolution</string>

      <string id="Console_ConnFixedResolution">Fixed resolution</string>
      <string id="Console_ConnFixedResolution_Help">Fixes this setting for every connection on this PC. It wins over the global defaults, the folders and the connection, which keep their own value but don't use it; the connection editor shows it greyed out at every level. A settings file shared with PCs without this policy keeps working there as before.

Enabled: the value set here.

Disabled or Not configured: the user decides (default: 1920x1080).

