      <string id="Console_ConnUseAgent">Tools through the RemoteHub Agent</string>
      <string id="Console_ConnUseAgent_Help">Fixes this setting for every connection on this PC. It wins over the global defaults, the folders and the connection, which keep their own value but don't use it; the connection editor shows it greyed out at every level. A settings file shared with PCs without this policy keeps working there as before.

Enabled: PowerShell, files, registry, services and processes go through the agent.

Disabled: they go over PowerShell remoting, below a jump host too.

Not configured: the user decides (default: no).

"Allow the RemoteHub Agent" disabled wins over it.

Registry: UseAgent (REG_DWORD) = 1 or 0.</string>

      <string id="Console_ConnRemoteDesktopVia">Remote desktop through</string>
      <string id="Console_ConnRemoteDesktopVia_Help">Fixes this setting for every connection on this PC. It wins over the global defaults, the folders and the connection, which keep their own value but don't use it; the connection editor shows it greyed out at every level. A settings file shared with PCs without this policy keeps working there as before.

Enabled: the value chosen here.

Disabled or Not configured: the user decides (default: Automatic).

With RemoteHub Agent while "Allow remote desktop through the agent" is disabled, there is no remote desktop; Settings → Policies shows the conflict.

Registry: RemoteDesktopVia (REG_SZ: Automatic, Rdp, Agent).</string>
      <string id="Console_ConnRemoteDesktopVia_Automatic">Automatic – the agent if installed, otherwise RDP</string>
      <string id="Console_ConnRemoteDesktopVia_Rdp">RDP</string>
